-- CA_0308_s3_library_pilot_school_boards.sql
-- CA_0308: seat nine school boards (FL, TX, MD, VA, MN, CA) and two former Alpine (UT) members, so that the
--   board votes in the Season 3 library-books Stage 0 census can be attributed to people in the roster.
--   Author: Chris Andrews (CA_ namespace). Status: APPLIED to prod 2026-10-14 (operator OK Chris Andrews), after two
--   dry runs (BEGIN..ROLLBACK, counts unchanged after rollback). Re-run once after apply: no change (idempotent).
--   Deltas: +84 politicians, +60 offices, +84 office_terms, +8 G5420 polygons, +9 districts; offices_missing_terms
--   unflagged stays 239; check:reachability at baseline (nothing regressed).
--
-- WHY: the Stage 0 census (.planning/research/s3-pilot-library/stage0-census.md, workspace root) found 23 board
--   records with named per-member votes, but only Alpine UT members existed in essentials.politicians, so the
--   plan gate (>= 10 records attributable to a person in the roster) scored 1. These boards were never loaded.
--
-- MODEL (same as the Plano/Collin TX and Bend-La Pine OR boards): per board one government (LOCAL), one chamber,
--   one SCHOOL district on the board's whole TIGER 2024 UNSD polygon (mtfcc G5420, geo_id = GEOID = NCES LEAID),
--   one office per seat. Single-member-district boards (Escambia, Somerset, Loudoun, Virginia Beach, Chino Valley)
--   are put on the WHOLE district polygon -- the Alpine precedent -- so a resident sees the whole board, not only
--   their own member. Member-district polygons are not loaded here.
--   Polygons: www2.census.gov/geo/tiger/TIGER2024/UNSD/tl_2024_{12,24,27,48,51}_unsd.zip, full resolution,
--   coordinates rounded to 6 decimals. Chino Valley's polygon (0608460) was already loaded.
--
-- WHO: every CURRENT member (October 2026) is seated, so no seat lands in offices_missing_terms; FORMER members
--   are seated only where they voted on a census record and their seat is known. Sources are cited per term in
--   office_terms.source: board pages, the Maryland Manual, county elections offices, signed minutes; Ballotpedia
--   where no official page gives the date or seat (marked in the source text).
--   Honesty rules (CLAUDE.md): no invented dates. A first-known holder whose start no source gives is written with
--   term_start NULL / 'unknown'; a source that gives a month or year is written with that precision. Two gaps are
--   left unwritten on purpose: Loudoun Broad Run and Dulles 2024-2025 (holders not verified).
--   is_incumbent is explicit on every row: true for the 59 seated members, false for the 25 former members.
--   is_active = true for all (ruling 2026-09-24: former officeholders stay active).
--   Keller ISD Place 6 is vacant (Randklev resigned Dec 2025; special election 2026-11-03): vacate_office.
--
-- LEFT OUT (decided, not missed):
--   St. Francis Area Schools ISD 15 (MN): the district site blocks fetches; the current roster and the 4-3 vote
--     could not be confirmed from any official source.
--   Virginia Beach Manning and Anderson: both held pre-2022 at-large seats; which 2025 seat each became is not
--     stated by any source. Chino Valley Don Bridge and Jon Monroe: Bridge's area and Smith's appointment date were
--     not found. The census records of those boards still have >= 3 named voters seated without them.
--
-- ALPINE: Hacken and Bonner each get a closed term ending the day before their successor (Peterson 2025-01-06,
--   Lincoln 2023-01-02). Those successors' terms were backfilled with term_start NULL (an open range that overlaps
--   any earlier term), so their starts are dated first. Nothing else on the Alpine board changes.
--
-- Apply with: npx tsx scripts/_apply-file.ts <abs path>

BEGIN;

-- ═══ Escambia County School District (FL) · TIGER UNSD 1200510 · 5 seats ═══
